Vocabulary:
  # The scripted ground control agent (cognition_agent::ScriptedBrain) with the three computer
  # pilots: Kestrel (id 1, it), Merlin (2) and Swift (3).
  State: the chaser Kestrel is far from the others | behind Merlin and ahead of Swift | near Merlin
    Shows: far from the others: Kestrel is it, in the middle of the arena. Merlin is 70 m to the east, and Swift is 70 m to the west
    Shows: behind Merlin and ahead of Swift: Kestrel is it. Merlin is 40 m ahead of Kestrel and slower. Swift is 30 m behind Kestrel
    Shows: near Merlin: Kestrel is it. Merlin is 50 m to the east of Kestrel, and Swift is 75 m to the west
  State: the plane that Kestrel pursues is none | Merlin | Swift
    Shows: none: Kestrel gets no pursue plan
    Shows: Merlin: Kestrel gets a pursue plan with Merlin, id 2, as its target
    Shows: Swift: Kestrel gets a pursue plan with Swift, id 3, as its target
  State: the plan of Merlin is none | pursue | evade | go to | orbit | band | loiter
    Shows: band: Merlin gets a band plan
    Shows: evade: Merlin gets an evade plan
  State: the plan of Swift is none | pursue | evade | go to | orbit | band | loiter
    Shows: band: Swift gets a band plan
    Shows: evade: Swift gets an evade plan
  State: the band of Merlin is none | 20 to 30 m | 35 to 45 m | 50 to 58 m
    Shows: 35 to 45 m: the plan of Merlin gives the band from 35 m to 45 m above home
  State: the band of Swift is none | 20 to 30 m | 35 to 45 m | 50 to 58 m
    Shows: 50 to 58 m: the plan of Swift gives the band from 50 m to 58 m above home
  State: the pursue plans for the planes not it are 0..100000
    Shows: 0: the report of the runner says `RESULT pursue_not_it=0`. Only the plane that is it got pursue plans
  State: the planes in AGENT mode are 0..3
    Shows: 3: the report of the runner says `RESULT in_agent=3`. All three planes played in AGENT mode
  State: the refused commands are 0..100000
    Shows: 0: the report of the runner says `RESULT refused=0`. The planes accepted every plan, every [[game command]] and every mode change
  State: the reports of the hand-overs are complete | incomplete
    Shows: complete: for each new plane that is it, the runner printed a line. The line says who tagged whom, or who left the arena

  Event: the ground control agent decides
    Say: wait for the next decision of the ground control agent
  Event: the planes play a game of tag
    Say: scroll up to the report just above `console ready`

Feature: Tag by plan
  In a game of [[tag]], the scripted [[ground control agent]] flies the three [[computer
  pilot]]s by plan. It does what the computer pilots do in the simulator, but with plans. Each
  plane gets a new plan once a second. Each plan is good for 2.5 s.

  The plane that is [[it]] gets a [[pursue]] plan. The other planes get a [[band]] plan each,
  with a height band of their own: Kestrel from 20 m to 30 m, Merlin from 35 m to 45 m and Swift
  from 50 m to 58 m. The bands start 15 m apart, so that the planes do not meet by chance. When
  the chaser comes near, a plane gets an [[evade]] plan. A plane that flies out of the arena
  gets a [[go to]] plan back to the middle.

  The [[runner]] plays the game with three ArduPlane SITL planes. Start it with
  `SIM001_BIN=.ardupilot-agent/build/sitl/bin cargo run --release -p cognition_runner -- --agent --speedup 10`.
  The planes take off in QHOVER and change to FBWA at 15 m. Then the ground switches them to
  AGENT mode and flies the game. Every 2 s, the runner prints the plan of each plane, in a line
  such as `Kestrel  sys 1 AGENT plan Pursue->2 #12 30m`. At ten times real time, the game takes about
  25 s.

  Expectation: The plane that is it pursues the plane it can catch soonest
    The ground control agent estimates the time to catch each plane: the distance, divided by
    the speed that the chaser has more than the target. If the target is behind the chaser, it
    adds 3 s. Thus a slow plane ahead is a better target than a near plane behind. The chaser
    keeps its target until another target is clearly quicker to catch.

    Given the chaser Kestrel is behind Merlin and ahead of Swift
    When the ground control agent decides
    Then the plane that Kestrel pursues is Merlin

  Expectation: A plane that is not it holds its own height band
    Given the chaser Kestrel is far from the others
    When the ground control agent decides
    Then the plan of Merlin is band
    And the band of Merlin is 35 to 45 m
    And the plan of Swift is band
    And the band of Swift is 50 to 58 m

  Expectation: A plane that is not it breaks away from a chaser that comes near
    How far a plane sees the chaser depends on its pilot: Kestrel sees it at 80 m, Merlin at
    60 m and Swift at 40 m. The evade plan gives the band of the plane, but the executor flies
    20 m above or below the chaser. Thus an evade can take a plane out of its band.

    Given the chaser Kestrel is near Merlin
    When the ground control agent decides
    Then the plan of Merlin is evade
    And the band of Merlin is 35 to 45 m
    And the plan of Swift is band

  Expectation: A plane that is not it never pursues
    When the planes play a game of tag
    Then the pursue plans for the planes not it are 0

  Expectation: Every plane plays in AGENT mode and accepts every command
    When the planes play a game of tag
    Then the planes in AGENT mode are 3
    And the refused commands are 0

  Expectation: Each new plane that is it is reported
    The game changes who is it when the chaser tags a plane, or when a plane leaves the
    arena. The runner reports each change, and it says which of the two it was.

    When the planes play a game of tag
    Then the reports of the hand-overs are complete
